* sg13g2-lna -- matching-network feasibility study, CHARACTERIZATION deck
* (issue #186). Generated from
* sim/lna-matching-feasibility/testbench/tb_match_char.spice.tmpl by
* sim/lna-matching-feasibility/matching_solver.py (gen-char) -- do not edit a
* generated netlist-snapshots/*.spice file, edit this template and re-run.
* Full bench definitions: sim/lna-matching-feasibility/README.md.
*
* ONE PVT cell only: HBT_SECTION=hbt_typ MOS_SECTION=mos_tt TEMP=27 C
* VDD=1.80 V (the nominal cell). This is a single-corner exploration deck,
* not a PVT result.
*
* What it measures (the inputs the matching solver needs), all at 50 Ohm
* `sp` ports (portnum/z0 = 50, the lna-characterization convention):
*
*   A. per Le-loss case (@@CASE_LIST@@), with the committed Lc = 5 nH:
*      the DUT's in-band two-port S-parameters plus ngspice's two-port noise
*      parameters NFmin, Rn, SOpt (`sp ... 1`, donoise). NFmin is referenced
*      to the ANALYSIS temperature (300.15 K here); the solver re-references
*      to T0 = 290 K.
*   B. per Le-loss case, with Lc replaced by an ideal 1 uH RF choke: S22,
*      from which the solver backs out the device's own collector-node
*      admittance Ydev = Y_node - 1/(jw*1uH) after removing the in-series
*      100 pF Cout. Ydev is what the output network must transform.
*   C. an ideal-Le sweep at the band centre: input impedance and noise
*      parameters versus Le, i.e. how much of a lever degeneration is on
*      this DUT's input.
*   D. the three EM-extracted inductor geometries of
*      sim/models/sg13g2_inductor_em.spice as one-ports (la and sub at
*      ground, lb driven by a 1 A AC current source): Z(f) -> L and Q in band.
*
* DUT: design/netlist/lna.spice inlined verbatim except the edit marked
* 'BENCH EDIT' (a resistor in parallel with Le, so Le's loss can be altered
* without a DC drop; @@RIDEAL@@ Ohm stands for "ideal"). design/ itself is
* not modified.

.lib "@@MODELS_LIB@@" hbt_typ
.lib "@@MOS_LIB@@" mos_tt
.include "@@EM_MODEL@@"

.options temp=27 tnom=27 gmin=1e-10

@@DUT@@

* --- S-parameter branch (50 Ohm ports) -----------------------------------
Vdda vdda 0 dc 1.8
Vp1 pin 0 dc 0 ac 1 portnum 1 z0 50
Vp2 pout 0 dc 0 ac 0 portnum 2 z0 50
Xa vdda 0 pin pout lna

* --- EM inductor one-ports (isolated; la = sub = ground, lb driven) -------
@@EM_ONEPORTS@@

.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
set wr_singlescale
set wr_vecnames
option numdgt=10
op
let ic1 = @q.xa.xq1.qnpn13g2[ic]
let ic2 = @q.xa.xq2.qnpn13g2[ic]
let idd = -i(vdda)
echo "OP ic1 $&ic1 ic2 $&ic2 idd $&idd"

@@CHAR_CASES@@

@@LE_SWEEP@@

* --- D. EM inductor one-ports ---------------------------------------------
ac lin @@N_BAND@@ @@F_LO@@ @@F_HI@@
wrdata @@OUTDIR@@/char_em.dat @@EM_VECS@@
echo "DAT_WRITTEN char_em.dat"
echo "BENCH_COMPLETE"
.endc
.end
